{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "run": 3,
  "simulation_id": "sim-01",
  "chair_id": "pearce-mark",
  "model": "gpt-6-luna",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_luna_chair_summary_v1.md",
  "summary": {
    "leading_positions": [
      {
        "ballot_ids": ["B008"],
        "explicit_supporters": ["kroll-stefan", "lindroth-eva", "olsson-eva"],
        "synthesis": "All three prefer Katori and Ye for optical lattice clocks, emphasizing complementary foundational contributions, replication, and a durable precision measurement capability. Their proposed citations vary in emphasis, from clock development to invention and realization; they agree the award should focus on the foundational advance rather than later precision gains."
      },
      {
        "ballot_ids": ["B038"],
        "explicit_supporters": ["danielsson-ulf", "pearce-mark"],
        "synthesis": "Both prefer Halzen for the discovery and establishment of high-energy astrophysical neutrino astronomy. Their citations differ in wording, but both focus on the discovery. They regard an individual attribution as defensible while requiring scrutiny of whether Halzen's leadership was decisive relative to the collaboration's detector and discovery work."
      },
      {
        "ballot_ids": ["B015"],
        "explicit_supporters": ["mehlig-bernhard"],
        "synthesis": "Mehlig prefers Jarzynski, Evans, and Crooks for exact nonequilibrium relations, treating their related contributions as a coherent theoretical achievement. He asks for historical review of the boundary between the original results and later generalizations."
      },
      {
        "ballot_ids": ["B010"],
        "explicit_supporters": ["eriksson-olle"],
        "synthesis": "Eriksson prefers Moodera, Yuasa, and Parkin for room-temperature tunneling magnetoresistance in crystalline MgO junctions. He emphasizes the result's practical conditions and device relevance, while noting that Miyazaki's related work and the contributions of multiple groups require historical review."
      },
      {
        "ballot_ids": ["B046"],
        "explicit_supporters": ["johansson-goran"],
        "synthesis": "Johansson prefers Blais, Wallraff, and Schoelkopf for establishing circuit QED as a controllable regime of coherent light–matter interaction. He sees a focused theory–experiment attribution, while asking whether it draws too narrow a boundary around a field developed by many groups."
      }
    ],
    "areas_of_agreement": [
      "The B008 supporters agree that optical lattice clocks are experimentally mature, replicated across laboratories, and established as a lasting precision measurement method.",
      "The B008 supporters agree that recognition should center on Katori's and Ye's foundational contributions and avoid implying that they account for every later improvement in optical metrology."
    ],
    "scientific_disputes": [
      "The committee should weigh B038's established new observational channel and discovery against B008's completed measurement capability and its demonstrated precision uses; some fundamental tests and source identification remain ongoing.",
      "For B015, the dispute is how broadly the exact fluctuation and work relations have influenced physics beyond nonequilibrium statistical mechanics.",
      "For B010 and B046, the cases emphasize distinct results and platforms, while the committee must assess how far each can be separated from broader developments in spintronics or quantum circuits."
    ],
    "attribution_disputes": [
      "For B038, the key question is whether Halzen's role in initiating and sustaining IceCube was decisive enough for an individual award, given the essential work of detector teams and the wider collaboration.",
      "For B008, members agree on Katori and Ye but call for a defensible boundary between their foundational advances and subsequent contributions to optical frequency standards.",
      "For B010, the proposed three-person attribution leaves Miyazaki outside despite related work being recognized in the opening assessment; the relationships among the groups need examination.",
      "For B046, the committee must test whether the proposed theory–experiment attribution fairly represents the early work while distinguishing it from contributions by other groups."
    ],
    "maturity_disputes": [
      "B008 is described as a mature, repeatedly realized method, but members differ on whether the completed measurement capability alone makes a sufficiently bounded prize subject while some fundamental applications continue.",
      "For B038, continued source identification is relevant to the field's development, but its supporters argue that the established astrophysical neutrino detection is already a completed discovery and need not await resolution of every source."
    ],
    "conflict_or_recusal_flags": [
      "Johansson reports professional proximity to superconducting circuits through his work and WACQT leadership, and says whether this warrants recusal on B046 is unresolved."
    ],
    "questions_for_round2": [
      "What evidence establishes that Halzen's contribution to the first robust identification of an astrophysical neutrino flux was decisive, and how should the citation acknowledge the collaboration's essential work?",
      "What specific foundational advances by Katori and Ye should define the B008 citation, and where should it draw the line between those advances and later clock improvements?",
      "For B010, how do the contemporaneous contributions of Moodera, Yuasa, Parkin, and Miyazaki bear on the proposed three-person attribution?",
      "For B015, what historical and scientific basis supports treating the Evans, Jarzynski, and Crooks results as one coherent prize achievement, and how should their impact beyond statistical physics be assessed?",
      "Does Johansson's reported professional proximity to superconducting circuits require recusal from deliberation on B046?"
    ],
    "chair_observation": "Round 1 produced several distinct preferred achievements, with the clearest shared position around optical lattice clocks. The main questions for round 2 concern the boundary of the recognized contribution, the strength of individual attribution, and whether a mature capability or an established discovery best defines the prize subject."
  }
}
